/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  unsteady07_fast_tank_full -- two mixing tanks in series, a BIG one and a
  SMALL one, and the question every model of a plant meets: does the small
  one need to be integrated at all?

  THE PLANT.  A feed of 1e-3 kmol/s runs through SLOW (1 kmol held, time
  constant tau_s = 1000 s) and then FAST (0.05 kmol held, tau_f = 50 s).
  Both tanks start full of compA; from t = 0 the feed is pure compB, the
  tracer.  No reaction, no jacket: the two synthetic components (the
  unsteady02 pair, 30 kg/kmol each) carry nothing but their identity.

  THE FULL MODEL (this case).  Both tanks are vessels (`dynamicCSTR`), each
  integrated in time, so the outlet of FAST lags the outlet of SLOW by
  about tau_f.  Its twin unsteady08_fast_tank_reduced replaces FAST by its
  quasi-steady relation -- a tank that holds nothing that accumulates, so
  its outlet IS its inlet -- and the two answers differ by that lag alone.
  The ratio of the two time scales is

      eps = tau_f / tau_s = 0.05,

  and the largest gap between the two outlet tracer fractions is, in
  closed form for these two linear tanks,

      x_full(t) - x_red(t) = tau_f (e^(-t/tau_s) - e^(-t/tau_f)) / (tau_s - tau_f),

  whose maximum is eps^(1/(1-eps)) = 0.0428 here.  The EduTool page "When
  the fast obeys the slow" runs both cases with the small tank's holdup
  changed and draws that gap against eps.

  WHAT THE STEP COSTS.  The router hands SLOW's outlet to FAST once per
  driver step (one-step explicit, announced by the [routing] line), so the
  driver step must stay short against tau_f: 0.25 s is a 40th of the
  smallest tau_f the page uses (10 s), and the fixed RK4 step is stable
  only below 2.785 tau_f.  The reduced twin has no such limit from FAST.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

units
(
    {
        name        SLOW;
        type        dynamicCSTR;
        in          feed;
        outputs     ( s12 );
        operation
        {
            UA           0.0;             // W/K: no jacket
            T_jacket     330.0 K;
        }
    }
    {
        name        FAST;
        type        dynamicCSTR;
        in          s12;
        outputs     ( product );
        operation
        {
            UA           0.0;             // W/K: no jacket
            T_jacket     330.0 K;
        }
    }
);
